<h2 id="answer-key"><strong>Answer Key</strong></h2>
<ol>
<li>The remote PIC must determine that the aircraft and complete UAS are in a condition for safe operation before flight.</li>
<li>A repeatable checklist reduces omissions and helps prevent familiarity, distraction, or time pressure from causing critical steps to be skipped.</li>
<li>Examples include airframe/structure, control surfaces and linkages, propeller/motor, battery, payload, registration markings, avionics, antennas, controller, communications link, GPS/GNSS, and telemetry.</li>
<li>The aircraft is very close to Runway 36 and is about to land.</li>
<li>It substitutes standardized words for letters so transmissions are less likely to be misunderstood.</li>
<li>Roger means the transmission was received. Wilco means the message is understood and the speaker will comply.</li>
<li>Who you are calling, who you are, and what you want.</li>
<li>Those bands are shared with Wi-Fi and many other devices; obstacles and antenna orientation can also reduce signal quality.</li>
<li>Lost link is loss of the command-and-control link. Its predetermined behavior must be known so the crew can predict where the aircraft will go and manage the resulting risk.</li>
<li>A flyaway is an unintended loss of control in which the aircraft continues flying unpredictably. Loss of GPS may only remove navigation/position-hold functions while manual control remains available.</li>
<li>When continuing flight presents a greater hazard to people or other aircraft than intentionally ending the flight.</li>
<li>A self-heating battery reaction that can cause a cell to overheat, ignite, and spread heat to neighboring cells.</li>
<li>A systematic process for identifying hazards, evaluating risk, considering alternatives, and selecting a safe course of action.</li>
<li>The effective use of people, equipment, information, checklists, and other available resources before and during flight.</li>
<li>Anti-authority, impulsivity, invulnerability, macho, and resignation.</li>
<li>Not so fast—think first.</li>
<li>It can slow reaction time, reduce concentration and situational awareness, and increase errors and poor decisions.</li>
<li>A safe aircraft is not enough; an impaired, fatigued, stressed, dehydrated, or otherwise unfit pilot can make the operation unsafe.</li>
<li>Develop and document an appropriate maintenance and inspection procedure for the aircraft and track relevant component life and maintenance history.</li>
<li>“You have control.” and “I have control,” with acknowledgement so both people know who is flying.</li>
</ol>
